1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,848
BETA Cutting Room is free, open-source
software for garment factories. It runs in

2
00:00:04,848 --> 00:00:10,068
your browser, with no account. This is
the real browser app, using only synthetic

3
00:00:10,068 --> 00:00:14,133
sample patterns.
Let us follow three ways to start.

4
00:00:14,133 --> 00:00:18,841
First, a small unit with paper patterns.
Open Photo to marker. Photograph your

5
00:00:18,841 --> 00:00:24,273
pieces beside an A four sheet on a
flat surface. Here we load an original

6
00:00:24,273 --> 00:00:29,333
synthetic test image through the real
photo reader, not the practice button.

7
00:00:29,333 --> 00:00:34,422
Review each outline. Give it a name and
size. Check copies, pairs, fabric group

8
00:00:34,422 --> 00:00:39,510
and grain. Keep main fabric, lining, rib
and fusing separate. They can each have

9
00:00:39,510 --> 00:00:41,667
their own fabric settings.

10
00:00:41,667 --> 00:00:46,390
Before cutting real cloth, check a
distance against your paper pattern with a

11
00:00:46,390 --> 00:00:51,114
tape. Choose two points, enter the measured
distance and review the difference. A

12
00:00:51,114 --> 00:00:55,467
clean test image does not prove
accuracy on factory photographs.

13
00:00:55,467 --> 00:01:00,904
Set the fabric width and how many garments
you need. Make the marker. The real

14
00:01:00,904 --> 00:01:05,254
nesting engine places the accepted pieces
across the fabric. Review the result

15
00:01:05,254 --> 00:01:09,967
before printing, and save your
pattern set for the next order.

16
00:01:09,967 --> 00:01:14,809
Second, the pattern master. This sample
tour starts from the T-shirt block. The

17
00:01:14,809 --> 00:01:20,397
pattern is a starting draft, not a
promise of fit. Edit the style for your

18
00:01:20,397 --> 00:01:23,733
customer, then sew a
sample before production.

19
00:01:23,733 --> 00:01:29,180
Grade from the size chart. Here the same
style has small, medium, large and extra

20
00:01:29,180 --> 00:01:33,537
large sizes. Review the graded outlines
and seam checks. Changing a measurement

21
00:01:33,537 --> 00:01:37,900
changes the draft, so check
your work again after editing.

22
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:42,610
Third, the cutting room. Choose the
fabric width and lay. Set layers, face

23
00:01:42,610 --> 00:01:46,594
direction and garment rules.
Open, folded and tube fabric need different

24
00:01:46,594 --> 00:01:51,667
treatment. Gaps and stripe matching
also affect how the pieces can fit.

25
00:01:51,667 --> 00:01:56,747
Now make the marker. You are watching
the actual search, at its recorded speed.

26
00:01:56,747 --> 00:02:02,191
The layout updates as a better result
arrives. You can stop and keep the best

27
00:02:02,191 --> 00:02:07,267
result so far. Review the length, fabric
use and validation before cutting.

28
00:02:07,267 --> 00:02:11,987
The cut view shows marker length,
layers, passes and fabric needed for this

29
00:02:11,987 --> 00:02:17,070
sample. Use the cut plan for the whole
order. From there, continue to rolls,

30
00:02:17,070 --> 00:02:21,433
spreading sheets, bundles and
tickets as your cutting room needs.

31
00:02:21,433 --> 00:02:26,647
Export plotter files, DXF and full-size
or tiled PDF files from the browser. Here

32
00:02:26,647 --> 00:02:31,861
we actually download three sample files.
Test a small file on your own plotter

33
00:02:31,861 --> 00:02:37,033
first. These files do not prove
support for every cutter or machine.

34
00:02:37,033 --> 00:02:42,483
BETA is young and not perfect. It does not
establish a general win over commercial

35
00:02:42,483 --> 00:02:47,569
CAD. Folded and tube jobs still need
care. Real photo accuracy, fit and machine

36
00:02:47,569 --> 00:02:52,267
compatibility need more factory testing.
Always check a sample before production.

37
00:02:52,267 --> 00:02:57,334
Help us improve it. Open Feedback and
describe what went wrong, what you expected

38
00:02:57,334 --> 00:03:02,763
and the steps to repeat it. Share files
only if you have permission. Nothing is

39
00:03:02,763 --> 00:03:08,533
sent until you choose to send it.
Try the sample tour on the website.
